{"caller": "codex", "commit": "cf763a7dedf107bfa7fc4bb5149ea1e361e8d8ec", "date": "2026-10-06T09:19:57+00:00", "exit": 0, "files": ["conformance/corpus.py", "conformance/freeze_corpus.py", "conformance/native_record.py", "conformance/native_replay_report.py", "docs/conformance-progress.md", "docs/upstream-pilot.md", "justfile", "plans/20261006-native-replay-storage.status.md", "plans/20261006-native-replay-storage.task.md", "tests/test_native_replay_storage.py", "tools/check_resources.py"], "findings": [{"id": "20261006T091957Z-cf763a7d#1", "line": 106, "path": "conformance/corpus.py", "rule": "R1", "severity": "should", "text": "The CLI error message hard-codes the \"10 GiB\" capacity policy, which `tools/check_resources.py` already defines as `MIN_FREE_BYTES`, so the two can drift apart. Fix: build the message from `MIN_FREE_BYTES`, or let `check_resources` report the threshold."}, {"id": "20261006T091957Z-cf763a7d#2", "line": 21, "path": "conformance/native_replay_report.py", "rule": "R1", "severity": "should", "text": "The default engine version `'3.51.0'` and the `'sqlite3-' + version` library-name rule are literals inside `bindings`, copied from the recorder's version selection. Fix: use one named definition with a docstring, shared with `native_record.py`, to choose the engine version and library name for a record."}, {"id": "20261006T091957Z-cf763a7d#3", "line": 85, "path": "conformance/freeze_corpus.py", "rule": "R10", "severity": "should", "text": "The message \"Native replay receipt requires explicit storage and a path outside capture and corpus\" does not tell the user what to do next. Fix: name the given receipt path and tell the user to supply `--temporary-root` and a receipt path outside the capture and output directories."}, {"id": "20261006T091957Z-cf763a7d#4", "line": 182, "path": "conformance/freeze_corpus.py", "rule": "R11", "severity": "should", "text": "No test covers the changed freezer CLI: the required `--temporary-root`, the `check_resources` refusal, and the receipt name that is derived from `--output`. The tests call only `freeze()` directly. Fix: add a subprocess test with a timeout that checks the refusal without `--temporary-root` or with bad storage, and checks the location of the `<output>-native-replay.json` receipt."}, {"id": "20261006T091957Z-cf763a7d#5", "line": 51, "path": "tests/test_native_replay_storage.py", "rule": "R12", "severity": "should", "text": "`fresh = []` has no type hint. Fix: annotate it as `fresh: list[dict[str, Json]] = []`."}], "id": "20261006T091957Z-cf763a7d", "kind": "review", "reviewer": "claude", "revision": "cf763a7d", "rules": {"R1": "62d446279093", "R10": "638d8cbd1df8", "R11": "5de19cdbbbc1", "R12": "99f66579f467", "R13": "da0926dafb88", "R2": "e5e78fb2a52a", "R3": "4f9188eadd60", "R4": "ea7ca17539eb", "R5": "b8613a2d693b", "R6": "5600dce59aef", "R7": "0b68df581c57", "R8": "b4168359c60d", "R9": "5a69196344d0"}, "well_formed": true}
